# L §4.1 "An open index gets its keys from the rows of inputs keyed by it ... A key exists from the earliest known of
# the versions whose rows bring it, so an earlier cut doesn't see it"; L §5.10 a place keyed by an index is one place
# per key.  acct_rank's rows bring a1 (known 2026-01-01) and a2 (known 2026-05-01): sub[a1] opens at 100.00 PLN,
# sub[a2] at 50.00 PLN.  As known 2026-03-01 the index has one key and one keyed place.
=== m.tally
model op
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index accts: open
input acct_rank[a in accts]: int
place sub[a in accts]: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  acct_rank[a1] = 1
  opening[sub[a1]] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start

version v2
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-05-01
  acct_rank[a2] = 2
  opening[sub[a2]] = 50.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start

ask q1: bal(sub[a], 2026-12-31) for a in accts
ask q2: count(a in accts) as known 2026-03-01
ask q3: bal(sub[a], 2026-02-28) for a in accts as known 2026-03-01
=== expect
q1 (a = a1): 100.00 PLN
  cut 2026-10-20
q1 (a = a2): 50.00 PLN
  cut 2026-10-20
q2: 1
  cut 2026-03-01
q3 (a = a1): 100.00 PLN
  cut 2026-03-01
